WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.934
[music playing]

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:03.503
WIL WILLIS: Josh,
Ray, congratulations.

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:05.271
You're both one step closer to
the title of "Forged in Fire"

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:08.207
champion and that
check for 10 grand.

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:10.610
When you came here, you
used our tools and equipment

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.978
to make your blades.

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:13.213
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:14.981
where you will have
five days to make

00:00:15.047 --> 00:00:17.216
an iconic weapon from history.

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:19.018
Are you ready to see
what that weapon is?

00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:19.852
- Yes.
- Oh, yeah.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:20.686
Yeah.

00:00:20.786 --> 00:00:21.154
WIL WILLIS: All right.

00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:24.257
The panabas.

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:24.791
 OK.

00:00:27.426 --> 00:00:29.496
WIL WILLIS: Known as a chopping
tool for both agriculture

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:31.965
and combat, the panabas
earned its place

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:34.133
as a weapon of war in
the southern Philippines

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.701
during the 19th century.

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:38.972
Its sharp, forward curved blade
acted like an oversized meat

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:41.340
cleaver and delivered
deep, clean cuts, which

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:43.643
made it ideal for executions.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.212
On the battlefield,
warriors carrying a panabas

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:47.513
would follow behind
the front line

00:00:47.613 --> 00:00:50.616
to behead anyone unlucky
enough to have survived

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:53.052
the first wave of attacks.

00:00:53.152 --> 00:00:55.621
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:56.823 line:7%
 See you in five days.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.359 line:7%
[music playing]

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:01.794 line:7%
JOSH WESTON: Let's get it lit.

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:05.932
I'm home, I'm prepped, and
I'm ready to build a panabas,

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:08.334
a weird looking blade.

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.069
I'm not even sure
how to describe it,

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:11.670
and I've certainly
never built one.

00:01:11.737 --> 00:01:15.308
It's always so much fun to
watch it squish in the press.

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:19.112
My plan is to put some of
the fancier elements to it.

00:01:19.178 --> 00:01:20.980
[machine whirring]

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.915
Ah [bleep].

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:26.352
My press has seized up.

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:28.154
This is one of those
things that could

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:31.090
be a devastating
three-hour fix, and I

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:33.125
have to have this machine.

00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:35.394
It's one of those things
that I haven't had

00:01:35.494 --> 00:01:38.364
to deal with in about a year.

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:40.466
Of course, as soon
as I come home

00:01:40.566 --> 00:01:45.138
to do the final round something
like this has to happen.

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:49.876
I have to fix this, or I may
just lose the entire day.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:57.283
RAY KIRK: The most challenging
thing today is to get

00:01:57.349 --> 00:01:59.352
my blade ready for heat treat.

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:00.119
Ooh!

00:02:00.185 --> 00:02:01.254
Watch that torch.

00:02:05.624 --> 00:02:07.293
Not bad.

00:02:07.359 --> 00:02:11.363
Building the panabas
has been extremely fast.

00:02:11.463 --> 00:02:15.701
Got it all tempered, the
handle attached, bark shaped.

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:20.773
This is wet rawhide to keep
everything pretty solid.

00:02:20.873 --> 00:02:25.544
And if everything holds
together good we'll put the--

00:02:25.644 --> 00:02:26.946
rats.

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:30.315
The rawhide, it broke.

00:02:30.382 --> 00:02:33.085
Then I didn't really
have enough to finish it.

00:02:33.185 --> 00:02:36.356 line:0%
So I pulled the threads
out of some paracord

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:39.459 line:0%
and I made sure that I had
enough to go from one end

00:02:39.526 --> 00:02:40.926 line:7%
to the other.

00:02:40.993 --> 00:02:44.564 line:7%
 Ah, who's back in action?

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:47.400
I need to make up for some
lost time from yesterday,

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:50.202
so I'm going to spend
the day forging and just

00:02:50.302 --> 00:02:52.772
smoothing out all the bumps.

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:55.774
She's starting to slim out.

00:02:55.874 --> 00:02:57.177
Rough grind done.

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:02.347
 I plan to test
the edge of my knife

00:03:02.414 --> 00:03:03.749
cutting some saplings down.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:06.686
And I stole my dog's bone
and I'm going to chop

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:07.954
that to see how it works.

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:09.855
[dog whining]

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:13.426
[dramatic music]

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:16.863
Now for the bone chop.

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:24.070
That's my baby.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:26.272
It performed excellent.

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:30.209
This particular challenge went
exceptionally fast for me.

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:34.914 line:0%
Now it's time to relax
for a little bit.

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:37.417
 I have wood prepped
for my handle,

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:39.485
and I have it epoxied
together, but I

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:41.654
still don't have
anything close to looking

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:43.423
like a finished handle.

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:47.993
But what I'm going to do is
test it to see if it's strong

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:51.163
or not before I
do anything else.

00:03:51.263 --> 00:03:53.532
This test is a make or
break moment for me.

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:58.771
If it doesn't pass I've
essentially lost two days.

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:02.008
[dramatic music]

00:04:04.009 --> 00:04:05.711
Damn, I like this sword.

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:07.380
DOUG MARCAIDA: This
is the KEAL test

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:10.449
to see what kind of lethal
damage your panabas will do.

00:04:10.549 --> 00:04:13.185
I will take your weapon
and deliver slashes

00:04:13.252 --> 00:04:15.153
across this pig carcass.

00:04:15.254 --> 00:04:16.522
Josh, you're up first.
You ready?

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:17.055
 Absolutely.

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:19.024
[dramatic music]

00:04:19.091 --> 00:04:22.028
[hacking]

00:04:26.732 --> 00:04:27.733
Yes.

00:04:27.833 --> 00:04:28.801
DOUG MARCAIDA: OK, Josh.

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:30.636
This is a scary weapon.

00:04:30.702 --> 00:04:34.173
It's got a sweet spot in there
that allows for a nice chop,

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:38.411
and of course second chop
cut through the spine,

00:04:38.511 --> 00:04:40.813
the ribs, everything.

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:44.250
Your panabas will KEAL.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:45.784
Good job.

00:04:45.851 --> 00:04:47.452
RAY KIRK: Good job.
DOUG MARCAIDA: All right, Ray.

00:04:47.519 --> 00:04:48.721
It's your turn.
You ready?

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:49.589
 You betcha.

00:04:49.655 --> 00:04:51.490
DOUG MARCAIDA: Let's do this.

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:55.494
RAY KIRK: I'm thinking, I just
got to do as good as Josh did.

00:04:55.594 --> 00:04:59.231
But I loved it when Doug
said "It will KEAL."

00:04:59.298 --> 00:05:01.233
That's with two E's.

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:05.371
[dramatic music]

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:14.280
DOUG MARCAIDA: I need
me a cup of coffee, Ray.

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:15.048
 You betcha.

00:05:16.481 --> 00:05:18.383
 In the feel of this,
I can feel the blade

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:20.185
already wanting to chop.

00:05:20.252 --> 00:05:23.389
The arc is right where
the sweet spot is.

00:05:23.456 --> 00:05:27.092
That allows the blade to cut
cleanly all the way through.

00:05:27.193 --> 00:05:30.729
And overall your
panabas will KEAL.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:31.797
 My favorite.

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:33.599
DOUG MARCAIDA: Next
up is strength test.

00:05:33.699 --> 00:05:35.601
Dave?

00:05:35.701 --> 00:05:38.838
DAVID BAKER: Gentlemen, in 1521
the explorer Magellan landed

00:05:38.938 --> 00:05:41.840
on the island of Cebu,
sparking several decades

00:05:41.907 --> 00:05:45.243
of conflict between the
Philippines and Spain.

00:05:45.344 --> 00:05:47.146
So to test your
panabas I'm going

00:05:47.213 --> 00:05:50.983
to strike a Spanish morion twice
with the edge of your weapon.

00:05:51.049 --> 00:05:54.620
Now, this is not about what
your weapon does to the helmet,

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:58.057
but what the helmet
does to your weapon.

00:05:58.124 --> 00:05:58.857
Josh, you're up.

00:05:58.924 --> 00:05:59.758
You ready?

00:05:59.858 --> 00:06:00.292
 Sure.

00:06:00.359 --> 00:06:02.194
DAVID BAKER: OK.

00:06:02.261 --> 00:06:05.765
[music playing]

00:06:08.867 --> 00:06:11.738
[thunks]

00:06:22.014 --> 00:06:24.450
I don't see any wrinkling,
any deformation,

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:27.687
any rolling upon your edge,
which is pretty amazing.

00:06:27.753 --> 00:06:30.589
I put some dents in that helmet.

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:32.391
Ray, you ready for this?

00:06:32.491 --> 00:06:33.558
 Can't hardly wait.

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:34.660
DAVID BAKER: Let's
make it happen.

00:06:34.761 --> 00:06:37.997
[music playing]

00:06:39.632 --> 00:06:42.535
[thunks]

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:51.143
OK, Ray.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:53.312
I can see a little
shiny spot here.

00:06:53.379 --> 00:06:55.281
It's just that wire
edge feels like it's

00:06:55.381 --> 00:06:58.083
kind of tipped just a hair.

00:06:58.150 --> 00:06:59.785
It's definitely still sharp.

00:06:59.852 --> 00:07:00.519
It's very nice.

00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:01.854
It felt good in the hand.

00:07:01.954 --> 00:07:02.989
 Thank you.

00:07:03.055 --> 00:07:04.690
DAVID BAKER: Next up
is the sharpness test.

00:07:04.756 --> 00:07:06.626
For that I'll give
you back to Doug.

00:07:08.994 --> 00:07:11.664
DOUG MARCAIDA: Bladesmiths,
we know your blades can KEAL.

00:07:11.730 --> 00:07:13.332
We know your blades are strong.

00:07:13.399 --> 00:07:15.234
But are they still sharp?

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.303
To test the edge
retention of your blade,

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:19.572
I will take your panabas
and I will cut the rope.

00:07:19.638 --> 00:07:22.008
That will release
the sandbag, which

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:24.343
simulates an oncoming attack.

00:07:24.444 --> 00:07:28.480
I will then run the blade
across this and cut it.

00:07:28.581 --> 00:07:29.948
Josh, you're up first.
You ready?

00:07:30.015 --> 00:07:30.516
 Yes, sir.

00:07:30.583 --> 00:07:33.719
[music playing]

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:40.059
[sand spilling]

00:07:42.161 --> 00:07:44.730
 Yes.

00:07:44.831 --> 00:07:46.231
 Oh, he died.

00:07:46.331 --> 00:07:48.433
DOUG MARCAIDA: Me like the feel.

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:49.835
Feels good in the hand.

00:07:49.902 --> 00:07:53.672
Enough to move and maneuver
in close quarter combat.

00:07:53.739 --> 00:07:56.876
And overall, your
weapon will cut.

00:07:56.943 --> 00:07:58.243
 That's all I ever
wanted to hear!

00:07:58.310 --> 00:07:59.879
[laughter]

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:01.246
 Ray, it's your turn.

00:08:01.313 --> 00:08:02.180
You ready?

00:08:02.247 --> 00:08:03.182
RAY KIRK: You betcha?

00:08:03.248 --> 00:08:03.983
DOUG MARCAIDA: Let's do this.

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:05.150
 Let's do it.

00:08:05.251 --> 00:08:08.754
[music playing]

00:08:14.627 --> 00:08:17.730
[sand spilling]

00:08:20.065 --> 00:08:21.867
DOUG MARCAIDA: This is
going to be tough, Ray.

00:08:21.934 --> 00:08:22.635
 I know it.

00:08:22.735 --> 00:08:24.236
 I like your blade too.

00:08:24.336 --> 00:08:29.441
Your panabas definitely is a
cutter, and it's easy to wield.

00:08:29.508 --> 00:08:32.144
Your panabas will cut.

00:08:32.211 --> 00:08:32.945
 Thank you, sir.

00:08:33.045 --> 00:08:34.947
 Good job.

00:08:35.047 --> 00:08:36.815
WIL WILLIS: Josh and
Ray, I honestly hate

00:08:36.916 --> 00:08:39.151
that it's come to
me to be the guy

00:08:39.251 --> 00:08:40.486
that has to say these words.

00:08:40.552 --> 00:08:42.487
But there can only be
one "Forged in Fire"

00:08:42.554 --> 00:08:44.590
champion in this arena.

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:55.033
And that champion is Josh.

00:08:55.133 --> 00:08:59.005
Ray, unfortunately your
panabas did not make the cut.

00:08:59.105 --> 00:09:00.872
Jason Knight will explain.

00:09:00.972 --> 00:09:03.175
JASON KNIGHT: When it comes down
to this type of competition,

00:09:03.276 --> 00:09:05.444
sometimes just
the little details

00:09:05.511 --> 00:09:06.946
are the game changer, Ray.

00:09:07.012 --> 00:09:10.182
Josh had a little bit more
subtleties in his design.

00:09:10.283 --> 00:09:12.418 line:0%
His handle was
octagonally facet,

00:09:12.485 --> 00:09:15.154 line:0%
and he had file
work in the spine.

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:19.525
And those subtle details are
the reason why Josh's blade won.

00:09:19.592 --> 00:09:22.828
WIL WILLIS: Ray, please
surrender your weapon.

00:09:22.928 --> 00:09:23.461
 Buddy.

00:09:23.528 --> 00:09:24.230
 You got it.

00:09:24.297 --> 00:09:25.330
 Give me a hug.

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:26.799
[inaudible]

00:09:26.865 --> 00:09:28.834
RAY KIRK: Well, I feel great.

00:09:28.901 --> 00:09:32.271
I came here not
to prove anything.

00:09:32.337 --> 00:09:35.207
I just enjoy the competition.

00:09:35.307 --> 00:09:39.178 line:0%
My knife performed and his knife
performed, so he got the money

00:09:39.244 --> 00:09:39.946 line:7%
and I got the fun.

00:09:42.481 --> 00:09:43.649
 Josh, congratulations.

00:09:43.749 --> 00:09:45.017
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion

00:09:45.083 --> 00:09:47.887
and will be receiving
a check for $10,000.

00:09:47.953 --> 00:09:49.655
You're super excited
right now, aren't you?

00:09:49.722 --> 00:09:51.123
 This is, like--

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:54.126
it just feels so good.

00:09:54.193 --> 00:09:58.163
All of you fans, wherever the
hell you came from, I [bleep]

00:09:58.230 --> 00:09:59.798
love you guys.

00:09:59.865 --> 00:10:02.868
Josephine with her designs that
helped me get through round two

00:10:02.968 --> 00:10:05.270
with the handle, thank you.

00:10:05.337 --> 00:10:07.372
You made Daddy win.

00:10:07.473 --> 00:10:10.375
I am the "Forged
in Fire" champion!

00:10:10.476 --> 00:10:12.077
That's what the
[bleep] happened!

00:10:12.144 --> 00:10:13.345
Woo!

00:10:13.445 --> 00:10:15.547
[bleep] Sorry, Aunt Edie.

00:10:15.614 --> 00:10:18.284
[music playing]

